ngine/godot/pulls/124170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124170","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124170.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124170.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-06T17:11:06Z"},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n- Closes #124154\r\n\r\nFixes a regression where the script tooltip pops up outside the editor if you hover over a symbol and quickly move your mouse out of the text area. \r\n\r\nThis issue started in `f27afd713d` which introduced a new `hover_tooltip_timer` in `ScriptTextEditor` to show errors and warnings. \r\nThe problem is that the timer was only being canceled when the mouse left the entire `ScriptTextEditor` container, which often fails to catch the exit event if you move the cursor out of the text box really fast.\r\n\r\nThe fix is simple: we just stop the timer using the internal `CodeEdit`'s `mouse_exited` signal instead, which fires reliably the moment the mouse leaves the text area. \r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n### Before:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b026e34-c544-4b98-ac7e-f198ffde0b51\r\n\r\n### After:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/774afbc9-ecae-4848-9ec8-b6caae0f9da7\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","closed